&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;White House press secretary Katie Zacharia has been fired less than a week after taking up the post, two US officials said on Friday, following a turbulent start marked by questions over her legal credentials and criticism of her media appearances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zacharia was &quot;let go&quot; and is &quot;transitioning out&quot; of the position, news agency Reuters reported, citing two White House officials. Her departure leaves President Donald Trump without a key spokesperson just over two weeks before the November midterm elections, when his administration is seeking to highlight its achievements and help Republicans retain control of Congress.&lt;/p&gt;
